# answered by claude-opus-5-5, prompt /lib/phil/senses b350a3107fa4, 2026-10-19
benefit	one
citizens_good	one
# "good" appears in S3 both as external goods (money, office, power) and as goodness of mind. Only the second, moral goodness, is in citizens_good, and P2 and C both use it that way.
# P1 reads S1's "same end in view" (a shared aim) as "of use", and P2 reads S3 as being about usefulness. The claim's wording blends the two, but both statements take it as treatment that actually benefits the citizens.
